From e3db3636c5a1421439dde916d22a851ea5e32863 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daviesluo <daviesluo@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 16:32:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Tell what Polymarket pays apart per path, so a live
 mid-pool's rewards never land in mini-pool's readout.
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both paths quote from one account and Polymarket pays the account. Each path now books a
payout only for a market its own minutes show it quoting live that day, and mid-pool reads
the account's earnings only once it is live. No dry-run decision changes: mid-pool runs
through the changed path beside a byte copy of the path its pre-registration froze.

Kept off main on Davies' word (2026-10-04, "之后再部署吧…具体时间我来定，代码你先都存好"):
it redeploys the live order path, which waits for his decision on mid-pool's go-live.

Rebuilt on 51cd7e45 (2026-10-04's formula fix and mini-pool's book-quality rule): the comparison
with the path mid-pool froze takes the fix's own fields out of both sides first, as
pm_mid_formula.test.ts states them, so it still shows this change alone.
